  "prefLabel": "Ins 206.14 Consolidation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 206.14 Consolidation. Upon motion or the hearing officer’s own initiative, if 2 or more proceedings involve common questions of law or fact, and the hearing officer determines consolidation is fair and efficient, the hearing officer shall consolidate those proceedings for hearing, decision, or both, after providing the parties notice and an opportunity for hearing on the proposed consolidation.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
